WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:04.770
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute Papers
with Dr. Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:08.750
Today I am so excited to show you this.

00:00:08.750 --> 00:00:09.750
Look.

00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:18.099
We are going to have an AI look at 650 million
images on the internet, and then, ask it to

00:00:18.099 --> 00:00:22.919
generate the craziest synthetic images I have
ever seen.

00:00:22.919 --> 00:00:29.250
And wait, it gets better, we will also see
what this AI thinks it looks like.

00:00:29.250 --> 00:00:32.640
Spoiler alert - it appears to be cuddly.

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:33.859
You'll see.

00:00:33.859 --> 00:00:35.940
So what is all this about?

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:44.809
Well, in June 2020, OpenAI created GPT-3,
a magical AI that could finish your sentences,

00:00:44.809 --> 00:00:51.670
and among many incredible examples, it could
generate website layouts from a written description.

00:00:51.670 --> 00:00:58.710
This opened the door for a ton of cool applications,
but, note that all of these applications are

00:00:58.710 --> 00:01:01.579
built on understanding text.

00:01:01.579 --> 00:01:07.960
However, no one said that these neural networks
can only deal with text information.

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:15.210
And sure enough, a few months later, scientists
at OpenAI thought that if we can complete

00:01:15.210 --> 00:01:20.049
text sentences, why not try to complete images
too?

00:01:20.049 --> 00:01:23.409
And thus, Image-GPT was born.

00:01:23.409 --> 00:01:29.250
The problem statement was simple: we give
it an incomplete image, and we ask the AI

00:01:29.250 --> 00:01:31.970
to fill in the missing pixels.

00:01:31.970 --> 00:01:39.090
If we gave it this image, it understood that
these birds are likely standing on something.

00:01:39.090 --> 00:01:43.549
And it even has several ideas as to what that
might be!

00:01:43.549 --> 00:01:52.350
Look, a branch, a stone, or they can even
stand in the water, and, amazingly, even their

00:01:52.350 --> 00:01:55.620
mirror images are created by the AI.

00:01:55.620 --> 00:02:03.490
But then, scientists at OpenAI thought, why
not have the user write a text description,

00:02:03.490 --> 00:02:07.081
and get them a really well done image of exactly
that.

00:02:07.081 --> 00:02:13.980
That sounds cool, and it gets even cooler
the crazier the ideas we give to it.

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:19.730
The name of this technique is a mix of Salvador
Dalí and Pixar’s Wall-e.

00:02:19.730 --> 00:02:22.319
So please meet Dall-e.

00:02:22.319 --> 00:02:24.190
This could do a ton.

00:02:24.190 --> 00:02:29.740
For instance, this understands styles and
rendering techniques.

00:02:29.740 --> 00:02:35.239
Being a computer graphics person, I am so
happy to see that it learned the concept of

00:02:35.239 --> 00:02:42.600
low polygon count rendering, isometric views,
clay objects, and we can even add an X-ray

00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:45.090
view to the Owl.

00:02:45.090 --> 00:02:46.150
Kind of.

00:02:46.150 --> 00:02:49.930
And now, just a year later, would you look
at that!

00:02:49.930 --> 00:02:51.190
Oh wow.

00:02:51.190 --> 00:02:53.709
Here is Dall-e 2!

00:02:53.709 --> 00:03:00.540
Oh my, I cannot tell you how excited I am
to have a closer look at the results.

00:03:00.540 --> 00:03:02.220
Let's dive in together!

00:03:02.220 --> 00:03:04.340
So what can it do?

00:03:04.340 --> 00:03:07.260
Well, that’s not the right question.

00:03:07.260 --> 00:03:12.080
By the end of this video, I bet you will think
that the more appropriate question would be

00:03:12.080 --> 00:03:14.200
“what can’t it do”?

00:03:14.200 --> 00:03:19.989
This one can take descriptions that are so
specific, I would say that perhaps even a

00:03:19.989 --> 00:03:23.230
good human artist might have trouble with.

00:03:23.230 --> 00:03:29.130
Now, hold on to your papers, and have a look
at 10 of my favorite examples.

00:03:29.130 --> 00:03:30.130
1.

00:03:30.130 --> 00:03:35.000
“A panda mad scientist mixing sparkling
chemicals”.

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:37.799
Wow, look at that!

00:03:37.799 --> 00:03:39.360
This is something else.

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:46.379
It even has sunglasses for extra street cred,
and the reflections of the questionable substance

00:03:46.379 --> 00:03:50.010
it is researching are also present on its
sunglasses.

00:03:50.010 --> 00:03:51.010
A+.

00:03:51.010 --> 00:03:54.090
But the mad science doesn’t stop there.

00:03:54.090 --> 00:03:55.090
2.

00:03:55.090 --> 00:03:59.069
“Teddy bears mixing sparkling chemicals
as mad scientists”.

00:03:59.069 --> 00:04:05.610
But at this point, we already know that doing
this would be too easy for the AI.

00:04:05.610 --> 00:04:09.319
Let’s do it in multiple styles.

00:04:09.319 --> 00:04:18.030
First, steampunk, second, 1990s Saturday morning
cartoon, and third digital art.

00:04:18.030 --> 00:04:21.020
It can pull off all of these.

00:04:21.020 --> 00:04:22.020
3.

00:04:22.020 --> 00:04:24.200
Now, about variants.

00:04:24.200 --> 00:04:27.950
Give me "A teddybear on a skateboard in Times
Square."

00:04:27.950 --> 00:04:32.130
Now, this is interesting for multiple reasons.

00:04:32.130 --> 00:04:36.060
For instance, you see that it can generate
a ton of variants.

00:04:36.060 --> 00:04:38.480
That is fantastic.

00:04:38.480 --> 00:04:43.790
As a light transport researcher, I cannot
resist mentioning how nice of a depth of field

00:04:43.790 --> 00:04:48.470
effect it is able to make, and, would you
look at that!

00:04:48.470 --> 00:04:55.480
It also knows about highly sought-after signature
effect of the lights blurred into these beautiful

00:04:55.480 --> 00:04:57.920
balls in the background.

00:04:57.920 --> 00:05:04.080
The AI understands these bokeh balls and the
fact that it can harness this kind of knowledge

00:05:04.080 --> 00:05:06.170
is absolutely amazing.

00:05:06.170 --> 00:05:07.200
4.

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:11.520
And if you think that is too specific, you
have seen nothing yet.

00:05:11.520 --> 00:05:12.880
Check this out!

00:05:12.880 --> 00:05:20.030
“An expressive oil painting of a basketball
player dunking, depicted as an explosion of

00:05:20.030 --> 00:05:21.500
a nebula”.

00:05:21.500 --> 00:05:22.850
I love it.

00:05:22.850 --> 00:05:27.010
It also has a nice Space Jam quality to it.

00:05:27.010 --> 00:05:29.700
Well done, little AI.

00:05:29.700 --> 00:05:31.040
So good!

00:05:31.040 --> 00:05:32.040
5.

00:05:32.040 --> 00:05:33.040
You know what?

00:05:33.040 --> 00:05:36.690
I want even more specific, and even more ridiculous
images.

00:05:36.690 --> 00:05:44.690
“a propaganda poster depicting a cat dressed
as french emperor napoleon holding a piece

00:05:44.690 --> 00:05:45.690
of cheese”.

00:05:45.690 --> 00:05:48.520
Now that is way too specific.

00:05:48.520 --> 00:05:52.840
Nobody can pull that off…there is no way
that…wow!

00:05:52.840 --> 00:05:54.660
I think we have a winner here.

00:05:54.660 --> 00:05:58.620
When the next election is coming up, you know
what to do.

00:05:58.620 --> 00:05:59.620
6.

00:05:59.620 --> 00:06:03.730
And still, once again, believe it or not,
you have seen nothing yet.

00:06:03.730 --> 00:06:04.730
Yes, that’s right!

00:06:04.730 --> 00:06:06.770
We can even get more specific.

00:06:06.770 --> 00:06:11.650
So much so that we can even edit an image
that is already done.

00:06:11.650 --> 00:06:17.360
For instance, if we feel that this image is
missing a flamingo, we can request that it

00:06:17.360 --> 00:06:23.750
is placed there, but, we can even specify
the location for it.

00:06:23.750 --> 00:06:30.870
And, even the reflections are created for
it, and they are absolutely beautiful.

00:06:30.870 --> 00:06:36.910
Now note that I think that if there are reflections
here, then, perhaps there should have been

00:06:36.910 --> 00:06:39.290
reflections here too.

00:06:39.290 --> 00:06:44.630
A perfect test for one more paper down the
line, when Dall-e 3 arrives.

00:06:44.630 --> 00:06:49.590
Make sure to subscribe and hit the bell icon,
you really don’t want to miss it.

00:06:49.590 --> 00:06:50.600
7.

00:06:50.600 --> 00:06:55.070
This one puts up a clinic in understanding
the world around us.

00:06:55.070 --> 00:06:58.100
This image is missing something.

00:06:58.100 --> 00:06:59.180
Missing what?

00:06:59.180 --> 00:07:01.910
Well, of course, corgis.

00:07:01.910 --> 00:07:04.620
And, I cannot believe this.

00:07:04.620 --> 00:07:11.490
If we specify the painting as the location,
it will not only have a painterly style, but

00:07:11.490 --> 00:07:15.650
one that already matches the painting on the
wall.

00:07:15.650 --> 00:07:18.030
This is true for the other painting too.

00:07:18.030 --> 00:07:20.290
This is incredible.

00:07:20.290 --> 00:07:22.790
I absolutely love it.

00:07:22.790 --> 00:07:26.180
And, last test, does it?

00:07:26.180 --> 00:07:27.470
Yes it does!

00:07:27.470 --> 00:07:34.580
If we are outside of the painting at the photo
part, this good boy becomes photorealistic.

00:07:34.580 --> 00:07:39.320
Requesting variants is also a possibility
here, so, what do you think?

00:07:39.320 --> 00:07:41.640
Which is the best boy?

00:07:41.640 --> 00:07:43.380
Let me know in the comments below!

00:07:43.380 --> 00:07:45.480
And, number 8.

00:07:45.480 --> 00:07:52.760
If we can place any object anywhere, this
is an excellent tool to perform interior design.

00:07:52.760 --> 00:07:58.080
We can put a couch wherever we please, and
I am really looking forward to inspecting

00:07:58.080 --> 00:07:59.450
the reflections here.

00:07:59.450 --> 00:08:00.590
Oh yes.

00:08:00.590 --> 00:08:01.720
Oh yes.

00:08:01.720 --> 00:08:08.780
This is very difficult to compute - this is
not a matte, diffuse object, and not even

00:08:08.780 --> 00:08:14.850
a mirror-like specular surface, but a glossy
reflection that is somewhere inbetween.

00:08:14.850 --> 00:08:22.940
But it gets worse, this is a textured object,
which also has to be taken into consideration,

00:08:22.940 --> 00:08:28.860
and proper shadows also have to be generated
in a difficult situation where light comes

00:08:28.860 --> 00:08:31.090
from a ton of different directions.

00:08:31.090 --> 00:08:38.250
This is a nightmare, and the results are not
perfect, but my goodness, if this is not an

00:08:38.250 --> 00:08:44.170
AI that has a proper understanding of the
world around us, I don’t know what is.

00:08:44.170 --> 00:08:48.470
Absolutely incredible progress in just one
year.

00:08:48.470 --> 00:08:50.280
I cannot believe my eyes.

00:08:50.280 --> 00:08:52.060
You know what?

00:08:52.060 --> 00:08:53.060
Number 9.

00:08:53.060 --> 00:09:00.520
Actually, let’s look at how much it has
improved since Dall-e 1 side by side.

00:09:00.520 --> 00:09:03.250
Now there is no contest here.

00:09:03.250 --> 00:09:07.880
Dall-e 2 is on a completely different level
from its first iteration.

00:09:07.880 --> 00:09:13.900
This is so much better, and once again, such
improvement in just a year.

00:09:13.900 --> 00:09:15.510
What a time to be alive!

00:09:15.510 --> 00:09:21.580
And, what do you think Dall-e 3, if it appears,
will be capable of?

00:09:21.580 --> 00:09:25.020
What would you use this, or Dall-e 3 for?

00:09:25.020 --> 00:09:28.960
Please let me know in the comments below,
I’d love to know what you think.

00:09:28.960 --> 00:09:33.510
Now, of course, not even Dall-e 2 is perfect.

00:09:33.510 --> 00:09:34.760
Look at that.

00:09:34.760 --> 00:09:36.260
Number 10.

00:09:36.260 --> 00:09:41.120
Inspect the pictures and tell me, what do
you think the prompt for this must have been?

00:09:41.120 --> 00:09:42.410
What do you think?

00:09:42.410 --> 00:09:44.080
Not easy, right?

00:09:44.080 --> 00:09:46.700
Let me know your tips in the comments below.

00:09:46.700 --> 00:09:51.380
Well, it was “A sign that says deep learning”.

00:09:51.380 --> 00:09:57.660
Well, A+ for effort, little AI, but this is
certainly one of the failure cases.

00:09:57.660 --> 00:10:01.100
And, you know what, I cannot resist.

00:10:01.100 --> 00:10:02.150
+1.

00:10:02.150 --> 00:10:08.230
If you have been holding on to your papers,
now, squeeze that paper at least as hard as

00:10:08.230 --> 00:10:11.440
these scholars are squeezing their papers.

00:10:11.440 --> 00:10:13.750
So, which one are you?

00:10:13.750 --> 00:10:17.670
Which one resembles your reaction to this
paper the best?

00:10:17.670 --> 00:10:19.360
Let me know in the comments below.

00:10:19.360 --> 00:10:24.360
And, yes, as promised, here is what it thinks
of itself.

00:10:24.360 --> 00:10:28.930
It is very soft and cuddly.

00:10:28.930 --> 00:10:32.900
Or at least, it wants us to think that it
is so.

00:10:32.900 --> 00:10:34.080
Food for thought!

00:10:34.080 --> 00:10:39.960
And, if you speak robot and have any idea
what this writing could mean, make sure to

00:10:39.960 --> 00:10:41.920
let me know below.

00:10:41.920 --> 00:10:43.500
And one more thing.

00:10:43.500 --> 00:10:53.080
We noted that this AI was trained on 650 million
images, and uses 3.5 billion parameters.

00:10:53.080 --> 00:10:56.760
These are not rookie numbers by any stretch
of the imagination.

00:10:56.760 --> 00:11:02.940
However, I am hoping that with this, there
will be a chance that other, independent groups

00:11:02.940 --> 00:11:08.180
will also be able to train and use their own
Dall-E 2.

00:11:08.180 --> 00:11:14.370
Just in the last few years, OpenAI has already
given us legendary papers, for instance, an

00:11:14.370 --> 00:11:22.840
AI that can play hide and seek, solve math
tests, or play a game called DOTA 2 on a world

00:11:22.840 --> 00:11:24.650
champion level.

00:11:24.650 --> 00:11:31.420
Given these, I hereby appoint Dall-E into
the pantheon of these legendary works.

00:11:31.420 --> 00:11:39.870
And I have to say, I am super excited to see
what they come up with next.

00:11:39.870 --> 00:12:32.610
Thanks for watching and for your generous
support, and I'll see you next time!

